body:
Follow-up requested by the reporter (2026-11-11): **built-in stock vises and fixtures**, so common workholding doesn't need importing. Filed as sub-issues, all P2:
- **#788:** generic parametric milling vises, jaw widths 3, 4, 5, 6 and 8 in plus 100-200 mm, with the jaw opening set from the stock;
- **#787:** 5-axis self-centering vises (52, 75, 80, 125 mm), checked in tilted setups;
- **#789:** parallels, 1-2-3 and step blocks, strap clamps, soft jaws;
- **#790:** vendor vise STEP files, a user-guide page plus an import check with real downloads.
Lathe chucks and jaws stay with #744 (spun fixtures). The size table starts from public catalog figures and gets confirmed in #788 and #787.

Future direction from the user (2026-11-11), recorded rather than filed:
- built-in vises use standard sizes (#788 / PR #802), customised through their editable dimensions;
- users can bring vendor STEP files (#790);
- a later option is a **parametric vise as a SolidCraft project**, modelling an exact vise and exporting it. That waits for the maintainer's sign-off on SolidCraft work.

Fixture plates and modular workholding, requested by the user (2026-11-11), who runs this kit on their 770MX (a 770 XL grid plate, a microARC subplate and mod vises):
- **#819:** parametric fixture plates, with fixtures placed at grid holes and dowels;
- **#820:** modular plate-mounted vises;
- **#821:** a rotary subplate on the microARC A (it turns with the work and is counted in the swing check).
All use original generic geometry; the user's exact parts can be matched by measurement or vendor STEP (#790).
